WHAT HAS TO HAPPEN BEFORE RELEASE
---------------------------------

1. Choose the license. The paper's Artifact Description commits to "an
   OSI-approved license" (Appendix F, Availability). The candidates discussed
   were BSD-3-Clause (the most common default for ORNL research software),
   MIT, and Apache-2.0.

2. Clear it through UT-Battelle. This repository is work authored under
   contract DE-AC05-00OR22725 with the U.S. Department of Energy. Software
   release requires ORNL's software-release / IP review before publication,
   and the approved license text must be pasted here verbatim -- not
   paraphrased and not reconstructed from memory.

3. Record the assigned software disclosure or release number in NOTICE.

4. Replace this entire file with the approved text, then set the matching
   SPDX identifier in pyproject.toml (`license = { text = "..." }` or a
   `License ::` classifier, per the approved form).

